# Status block ids: SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH. Edit only this file.
#
# make derives both consumers from here in one step (tests/gen-status-ids.sh):
# - C: status-ids.h enum entries, included by barparse.h. Rebuild dwm as usual.
# - shell: contrib/status-ids.sh assignments, shipped to ~/.dwm by
#   `make install-ids` (only when the ids changed) and sourced by
#   ~/.dwm/dwm-status.sh (ST_*_BYTE block prefixes) and dwm-statuscmd.sh
#   (ST_* click keys, which match dwm's $INDEX). Restart the status daemon
#   afterwards.
# tests/check-status-ids.sh (in `make test`) fails loudly on any drift.
#
# Format: <Name> <decimal-id>, one per line. Name becomes St<Name> in C
# and ST_<UPPER> in shell. Id = the control character prefixing the block
# on the wire; a click reports it back as $INDEX.
# Reserved* lines reserve a number without emitting it anywhere.
Date 1
Battery 2
Volume 3
Reserved4 4
Reserved5 5
Disk 6
Mem 7
Cpu 8
Weather 9
Mpd 10
Net 11
Mail 12
Rss 13
Singbox 14
Notify 15
Screencast 16
